t=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Janakpur\\\" title=\\\"Janakpur\\\" id=\\\"mwQQ\\\">Janakpur<\\/a>, and <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Kathmandu\\\" title=\\\"Kathmandu\\\" id=\\\"mwQg\\\">Kathmandu<\\/a>, the diaspora celebrates Chhath to preserve their cultural heritage.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-9\\\" id=\\\"mwQw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwRQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwRA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">9<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwRg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-10\\\" id=\\\"mwRw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwSQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwSA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">10<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwSg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-11\\\" id=\\\"mwSw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwTQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwTA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">11<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwTg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-12\\\" id=\\\"mwTw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwUQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwUA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">12<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwUg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> The festival is also celebrated by the diaspora<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-13\\\" id=\\\"mwUw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwVQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwVA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">13<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwVg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-14\\\" id=\\\"mwVw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwWQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwWA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">14<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwWg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> in countries such as the United States, Australia, Singapore, Malaysia, the United Arab Emirates, Canada, Mauritius, Japan, and the United Kingdom.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-15\\\" id=\\\"mwWw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwXQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwXA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">15<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwXg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/p><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mwXw\\\">During Chhath <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Puja_(Hinduism)\\\" title=\\\"Puja (Hinduism)\\\" id=\\\"mwYA\\\">Puja<\\/a>, prayers are dedicated to the <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Solar_deity\\\" title=\\\"Solar deity\\\" id=\\\"mwYQ\\\">solar deity<\\/a>, <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Surya\\\" title=\\\"Surya\\\" id=\\\"mwYg\\\">Surya<\\/a>, to express gratitude for the blessings of life on Earth and to seek the fulfilment of personal wishes.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-16\\\" id=\\\"mwYw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwZQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwZA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">16<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwZg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> The Hindu goddess Chhathi Maiya (or <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhathi_Mata\\\" title=\\\"Chhathi Mata\\\" id=\\\"mwZw\\\">Chhathi Mata<\\/a>)\\u2014the sixth form of <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Prak%E1%B9%9Bti\\\" title=\\\"Prak\\u1e5bti\\\" id=\\\"mwaA\\\">Prakriti<\\/a> and Surya\'s sister\\u2014is also worshipped during the festival. It is celebrated for six days after <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Diwali\\\" title=\\\"Diwali\\\" id=\\\"mwaQ\\\">Deepavali<\\/a> or <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Tihar_(festival)\\\" title=\\\"Tihar (festival)\\\" id=\\\"mwag\\\">Tihar<\\/a>, until the sixth day of the <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Lunar_month\\\" title=\\\"Lunar month\\\" id=\\\"mwaw\\\">lunar month<\\/a> of Kartika (October or November) in the <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Hindu_calendar\\\" title=\\\"Hindu calendar\\\" id=\\\"mwbA\\\">Hindu calendar<\\/a> (<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Vikram_Samvat\\\" title=\\\"Vikram Samvat\\\" id=\\\"mwbQ\\\">Vikram Samvat<\\/a>), which is why it is called \'Surya Shashti Vrata\'.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-17\\\" id=\\\"mwbg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwcA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwbw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">17<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwcQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-18\\\" id=\\\"mwcg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwdA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwcw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">18<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwdQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-19\\\" id=\\\"mwdg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mweA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwdw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">19<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mweQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> The rituals are observed over three nights and four days,<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-20\\\" id=\\\"mweg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwfA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwew\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">20<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwfQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> and include holy bathing, fasting, abstaining from drinking water as a <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Vratta\\\" title=\\\"Vratta\\\" id=\\\"mwfg\\\"><i>vrata<\\/i><\\/a> (devotion), standing in water, and offering <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Prasada\\\" title=\\\"Prasada\\\" id=\\\"mwgQ\\\"><i>prasada<\\/i><\\/a> (prayer offerings of food) and <a class=\\\"mw-redirect\\\" style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Arghya\\\" title=\\\"Arghya\\\" id=\\\"mwgw\\\"><i>arghya<\\/i><\\/a> to the rising and setting of the Sun.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-21\\\" id=\\\"mwhA\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwhg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwhQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">21<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwhw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> Some devotees also perform a <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Prostration\\\" title=\\\"Prostration\\\" id=\\\"mwiA\\\">prostration<\\/a> march as they head towards the riverbanks.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-22\\\" id=\\\"mwiQ\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwiw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwig\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">22<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwjA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> All devotees prepare similar <i>prasada<\\/i> and offerings.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-23\\\" id=\\\"mwjg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwkA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwjw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">23<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwkQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-24\\\" id=\\\"mwkg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwlA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwkw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">24<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwlQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/p><div class=\\\"mw-heading mw-heading2\\\" style=\'color: rgb(16, 20, 24); font-family: \\\"Linux Libertine\\\", Georgia, Times, \\\"Source Serif 4\\\", serif; font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.375; margin: 0.25em 0px; padding-bottom: 0.17em; padding-top: 0.5em\'><h2 style=\'border-width: 0px; color: inherit; font-family: \\\"Linux Libertine\\\", Georgia, Times, \\\"Source Serif 4\\\", serif; font-size: inherit; line-height: 1.375; margin: 0px 0px 0.25em; padding: 0px\' id=\\\"Traditional_food_and_offerings\\\">Traditional food and offerings<\\/h2><\\/div><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mwmA\\\">Chhath Puja is also marked by the preparation and offering of a variety of traditional and <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Sattvic_diet\\\" title=\\\"Sattvic diet\\\" id=\\\"mwmQ\\\">sattvic<\\/a> (pure and vegetarian) dishes that are cooked without onion or garlic. These food items hold cultural and religious importance, often passed down through generations.<\\/p><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mwmg\\\">Four of the most important traditional prasadas (offerings) offered during Chhath Puja are:<\\/p><ol style=\\\"margin: -0.5em 0px 0px 3.2em; padding: 0px\\\"><li style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.1em\\\"><b><strong>Thekua<\\/strong><\\/b> \\u2013 A crispy, sweet snack made from wheat flour, <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Jaggery\\\" title=\\\"Jaggery\\\" id=\\\"mwng\\\">jaggery<\\/a>, and <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Ghee\\\" title=\\\"Ghee\\\" id=\\\"mwnw\\\">ghee<\\/a>, then deep-fried. Thekua is the most iconic offering of Chhath Puja.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-25\\\" id=\\\"mwoA\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwog\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwoQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">25<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwow\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/li><li style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.1em\\\"><b><strong>Rasabali<\\/strong><\\/b> \\u2013 A traditional dessert made from flattened rice soaked in sweetened milk, flavored with cardamom and dry fruits.<\\/li><li style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.1em\\\"><b><strong>Kasar (Laddoo)<\\/strong><\\/b> \\u2013 Made with powdered rice or wheat flour and jaggery, these laddoos are shaped into small balls and are considered a holy offering.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-26\\\" id=\\\"mwqA\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwqg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwqQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">26<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwqw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/li><li style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.1em\\\"><b><strong>Rice Laddu (Peethha)<\\/strong><\\/b> \\u2013 A steamed or fried dumpling filled with jaggery and coconut, especially common in Bihar and Eastern UP.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-27\\\" id=\\\"mwrg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwsA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwrw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">27<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwsQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/li><\\/ol><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mwsg\\\">These recipes are not only offerings but also symbolize purity, devotion, and cultural richness associated with the Chhath festival.<\\/p><div class=\\\"mw-heading mw-heading2\\\" style=\'color: rgb(16, 20, 24); font-family: \\\"Linux Libertine\\\", Georgia, Times, \\\"Source Serif 4\\\", serif; font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.375; margin: 0.25em 0px; padding-bottom: 0.17em; padding-top: 0.5em\'><h2 style=\'border-width: 0px; color: inherit; font-family: \\\"Linux Libertine\\\", Georgia, Times, \\\"Source Serif 4\\\", serif; font-size: inherit; line-height: 1.375; margin: 0px 0px 0.25em; padding: 0px\' id=\\\"Significance\\\">Significance<\\/h2><\\/div><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mwtA\\\">Chhath Puja is dedicated to <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Surya\\\" title=\\\"Surya\\\" id=\\\"mwtQ\\\">Surya<\\/a>, the Sun God, as it is thought that the sun is visible to every being and is the basis of life of all creatures on Earth.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-28\\\" id=\\\"mwtg\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwuA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwtw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">28<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwuQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> Chhathi Maiya (or Chhathi Mata) is also worshipped on this day. According to <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Hindu_astrology\\\" title=\\\"Hindu astrology\\\" id=\\\"mwug\\\">Vedic astrology<\\/a>, Chhathi Maiya grants children long life and good health by shielding them from illnesses and diseases.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-:0-29\\\" id=\\\"mwuw\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwvQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwvA\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">29<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwvg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/p><div class=\\\"mw-heading mw-heading2\\\" style=\'color: rgb(16, 20, 24); font-family: \\\"Linux Libertine\\\", Georgia, Times, \\\"Source Serif 4\\\", serif; font-size: 1.5em; line-height: 1.375; margin: 0.25em 0px; padding-bottom: 0.17em; padding-top: 0.5em\'><h2 style=\'border-width: 0px; color: inherit; font-family: \\\"Linux Libertine\\\", Georgia, Times, \\\"Source Serif 4\\\", serif; font-size: inherit; line-height: 1.375; margin: 0px 0px 0.25em; padding: 0px\' id=\\\"Description\\\">Description<\\/h2><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><p><a class=\\\"mw-file-description\\\" style=\\\"border-width: 0px; color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/File:Ranipokhari-IMG_3228.jpg\\\" id=\\\"mwwQ\\\"><img class=\\\"image_resized mw-file-element\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 0.666667px solid rgb(200, 204, 209); color: rgb(32, 33, 34); height: auto; margin: 3px; vertical-align: middle; width: 250px\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/thumb.wikimedia.org\\/wikipedia\\/commons\\/thumb\\/d\\/d5\\/Ranipokhari-IMG_3228.jpg\\/250px-Ranipokhari-IMG_3228.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\\\" alt=\\\"Rani Pokhari, a 17th-century pond in Kathmandu decorated with lights at night for Chhath celebration\\\" width=\\\"250\\\" height=\\\"167\\\"><\\/a><\\/p><div class=\\\"vector-body ve-init-mw-desktopArticleTarget-targetContainer\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(32, 33, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.625; text-align: start\\\" id=\\\"bodyContent\\\"><div><div><figure class=\\\"mw-default-size\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(248, 249, 250); color: rgb(32, 33, 34); float: right; line-height: 0; margin: 0.5em 0px 1.3em 1.4em; text-align: center\\\"><figcaption style=\\\"background-color: inherit; font-size: 14.144px; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 0px 6px 6px; text-align: start\\\">Chhath celebration (2015) at <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Rani_Pokhari\\\" title=\\\"Rani Pokhari\\\" id=\\\"mwxA\\\">Rani Pokhari<\\/a>, a 17th-century pond in <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Kathmandu\\\" title=\\\"Kathmandu\\\" id=\\\"mwxQ\\\">Kathmandu<\\/a><\\/figcaption><\\/figure><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><p><a class=\\\"mw-file-description\\\" style=\\\"border-width: 0px; color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/File:Chhath_Pooja_in_Delhi.jpg\\\" id=\\\"mwxw\\\"><img class=\\\"image_resized mw-file-element\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 0.666667px solid rgb(200, 204, 209); color: rgb(32, 33, 34); height: auto; margin: 3px; vertical-align: middle; width: 250px\\\" src=\\\"https:\\/\\/thumb.wikimedia.org\\/wikipedia\\/commons\\/thumb\\/f\\/f1\\/Chhath_Pooja_in_Delhi.jpg\\/250px-Chhath_Pooja_in_Delhi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\\\" width=\\\"250\\\" height=\\\"333\\\"><\\/a><\\/p><div class=\\\"vector-body ve-init-mw-desktopArticleTarget-targetContainer\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(32, 33, 34); font-family: sans-serif; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.625; text-align: start\\\" id=\\\"bodyContent\\\"><div class=\\\"mw-body-content\\\" style=\\\"margin-top: 16px\\\" id=\\\"mw-content-text\\\"><div class=\\\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\\\"><figure class=\\\"mw-default-size\\\" style=\\\"background-color: rgb(248, 249, 250); color: rgb(32, 33, 34); float: right; line-height: 0; margin: 0.5em 0px 1.3em 1.4em; text-align: center\\\"><figcaption style=\\\"background-color: inherit; font-size: 14.144px; line-height: 1.4em; padding: 0px 6px 6px; text-align: start\\\">Chhath celebrations happening at a temporary pond made for devotees in Shahdara, Delhi<\\/figcaption><\\/figure><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mwyg\\\">Chhath Puja is a <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/List_of_folk_festivals\\\" title=\\\"List of folk festivals\\\" id=\\\"mwyw\\\">folk festival<\\/a> that lasts four days. It starts with Kartik Shukla Chaturthi and ends with Kartik Shukla Saptami. Chhath is celebrated twice a year:<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-30\\\" id=\\\"mwzA\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwzg\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mwzQ\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">30<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mwzw\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/p><ol style=\\\"margin: -0.5em 0px 0px 3.2em; padding: 0px\\\"><li style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.1em\\\">Chaiti Chhath \\u2013 observed in the <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chaitra\\\" title=\\\"Chaitra\\\" id=\\\"mw0g\\\">Chaitra<\\/a> month of <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Vikram_Samvat\\\" title=\\\"Vikram Samvat\\\" id=\\\"mw0w\\\">Vikram Samvat<\\/a>.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-31\\\" id=\\\"mw1A\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mw1g\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mw1Q\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">31<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mw1w\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/li><li style=\\\"margin-bottom: 0.1em\\\">Kartik Chhath \\u2013 celebrated at a very large scale in the <a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Kartika_(month)\\\" title=\\\"Kartika (month)\\\" id=\\\"mw2Q\\\">Kartika<\\/a> month of Vikram Samvat.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-32\\\" id=\\\"mw2g\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mw3A\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mw2w\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">32<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mw3Q\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a><\\/li><\\/ol><p style=\\\"margin: 0.5em 0px 1em\\\" id=\\\"mw3g\\\">The main worshippers, called <i><span id=\\\"mw3w\\\">parvaitin<\\/span><\\/i> (transl.<span id=\\\"mw4g\\\">\\u2009<\\/span><span id=\\\"mw4g\\\">\'devotees\'<\\/span>, from Sanskrit <i>parva<\\/i>, meaning \'occasion\' or \'festival\'), are usually women. However, men also observe this festival as Chhath is not a gender-specific festival.<a style=\\\"color: rgb(51, 102, 204)\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\" href=\\\"https:\\/\\/en.wikipedia.org\\/wiki\\/Chhath#cite_note-33\\\" id=\\\"mw5A\\\"><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mw5g\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">[<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text\\\" id=\\\"mw5Q\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">33<\\/sup><\\/span><span class=\\\"mw-reflink-text cite-bracket\\\" id=\\\"mw5w\\\"><sup class=\\\"mw-ref reference\\\" style=\\\"font-size: 12.8px; line-height: 1\\\">]<\\/sup><\\/span><\\/a> The <i><span id=\\\"mw6A\\\">parvaitin<\\/span><\\/i> pray for the well-being of their family, and for the prosperity of their children.<\\/p><div class=\\\"mw-heading mw-heading3\\\" style=\\\"color: rgb(16, 20, 24); font-size: 1.2em; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0.25em 0px; padding-bottom: 0px; padding-top: 0.5em\\\"><h3 style=\\\"border-width: 0px; color: inherit; font-family: inherit; font-size: inherit; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0px 0px 0.25em; padding: 0px\\\" id=\\\"Nahaay_khaay_(day_1)\\\"><i><strong>Nahaay khaay<\\/strong><\\/i><strong> (day 1)<\\/strong><\\/h3><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div><\\/div>\"}]', 'D1', NULL, 1, '2026-10-23 09:12:23', '2026-10-23 09:12:23', '2026-10-23 09:12:23');
